  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, the case concerns whether attorney fees incurred in connection with filing a bankruptcy claim are recoverable as part of the claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Travelers Casualty and Surety Company",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Travelers Casualty and Surety Company, travelers argues that the Ninth Circuit's Fobian rule creates an unwarranted federal common\u2011law rule that exists outside the structure of the Bankruptcy Code."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Travelers Casualty and Surety Company",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Travelers Casualty and Surety Company, travelers contends that any right to payment, when the debtor files for bankruptcy, becomes a claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Travelers Casualty and Surety Company",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Travelers Casualty and Surety Company, travelers points out that when a bankruptcy plan says nothing, the default rule under Section\u202f1141(d) extinguishes the rights."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Travelers",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Travelers cites 28\u202fU.S.C.\u202f\u00a7\u202f502(b)(4) to argue that a claim for attorney services may be disallowed if it exceeds the reasonable value of those services."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Respondent argues that the Fobian rule is wrong, especially regarding the distinction it draws between state law and federal litigation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court notes that many cases allow attorneys\u2019 fees as unsecured claims."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court warns of an enormous amount of affirmative harm that could result if it overturns the Ninth Circuit\u2019s disallowance, and reserves an open question on the meaning of \u00a7\u00a7\u202f502(b) and\u202f506(b)."
      }
    ],
