                "start": 12
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Travelers Casualty and Surety Company, when a bankruptcy plan says nothing, the default rule in bankruptcy extinguishes the rights under Section\u202f1141(d)."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Travelers",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 38
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Travelers, section\u202f502(b)(4) allows a claim for attorney services only to the extent that the fees do not exceed the reasonable value of those services."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 56,
                "start": 56
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Brunstad, attorney fees have been allowed as unsecured claims for a century without causing disaster, indicating congressional acceptance of the practice."
        }
      ],
